  "configuration_id": "config_041",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most informative first experiment is a strong multimodal configuration to establish a performance ceiling and reduce uncertainty about whether the full multimodal pipeline (RNA + image) with powerful encoders is viable. config_041 combines scgpt (a pre-trained generative RNA encoder likely to capture rich transcriptomic structure), imagenet_vit_l (the strongest available image encoder), transformer aggregation (most expressive for multiprofile integration), and concat fusion (a standard, well-understood fusion strategy). This tests the core hypothesis that multimodal fusion with strong encoders outperforms simpler alternatives. It is the most expensive configuration (scgpt + ViT-L + transformer + multiprofile + multimodal), so I estimate its relative cost as ~1.0× (the reference maximum). Establishing this upper bound early is critical: if it performs strongly, subsequent experiments can explore cheaper variants (resnet50, avgpool, scvi_n200) to find a cost-effective sweet spot; if it underperforms, we immediately know the architecture needs rethinking, saving budget from chasing an unproductive direction. With 9 experiments remaining, this single expensive anchor gives the most leverage for the rest of the search."
}

